accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  13 removed_month 93 accessioned on  13 removed_month 93 at 18 51 clinical data  49 year old female status post left mammographic abnormality  read as infiltrating ductal carcinoma on needle biopsy                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  left   modified radical mastectomy  1  infiltrating ductal adenocarcinoma  grade removed_date  see note  with extensive lymphatic vascular invasion and multifocal involvement of the breast  removed_date axillary lymph nodes are positive for metastatic adenocarcinoma  there is extensive lymphatic involvement within the axillary fat  note  at least four separate foci of carcinoma are identified in the breast parenchyma  including areas that did not show gross evidence of tumor  examined inked margins are free of tumor  because of the multifocal involvement  the absence of an in situ component  and the recent history of metastatic carcinoma elsewhere  we favor the interpretation that this tumor is a metastasis from the left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen weighing 445 grams  the total specimen measures 25 x 13 x 3 5cm  the breast measures 16 x 13 x 2 5cm and the axillary tail measures 9 x removed_date x 1cm  overlying the specimen is a 17 x 6cm skin ellipse containing the nipple and a 4cm healed scar located inferolaterally to the nipple  located deep to this scar is a hard nodular  white to yellow area with central hemorrhage  this nodular area measures 4 x 3 x 2cm  it extends to within 0 6cm of the deep margin and 1cm of the inferior margin  located 7cm medially from the biopsy site and 4cm laterally from the medial resection margin is a 0 5cm hard  tan nodule  this nodule is 1 5cm beneath the skin surface and 2 5cm from the neasest resection margin which is the superior margin  sectioning of the ax